d mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8444em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mop\">lim</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1068em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mrel mtight\">→</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span></span></span></span> is the set of plot-connetced components of the diffeological space <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">X</span></span></span></span>.</p>","timestamp":1275642179,"subject":"diffeological spaces as a connected quasi-topos","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":11959,"sender_id":43,"sender_full_name":"DavidRoberts","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fbc2dbfb28f9e9275a4fd4cd109b5a21?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/diffeological.20spaces.20as.20a.20connected.20quasi-topos/near/11959\">#5</a> Cool, thanks.</p>","timestamp":1275644189,"subject":"diffeological spaces as a connected quasi-topos","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":11960,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/diffeological.20spaces.20as.20a.20connected.20quasi-topos/near/11960\">#6</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Cool,</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I like it, too. Of course it may not look like too deep a statement, but it is the tip of an iceberg: indeed I ran into the analog first for the (oo,1)-topos on CartSp.</p>\n<p>I am currently typing out more expositional notes on this <a href=\"http://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+an+(%E2%88%9E%2C1)-topos+--+survey#LocallyConnected\">here</a>.</p>","timestamp":1275645189,"subject":"diffeological spaces as a connected quasi-topos","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":11963,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/diffeological.20spaces.20as.20a.20connected.20quasi-topos/near/11963\">#7</a> Okay, I made this a section at <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/diffeological%20space\">diffeological space</a>: <a href=\"http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/diffeological+space#Connectedness\">Connectedness</a></p>","timestamp":1275680369,"subject":"diffeological spaces as a connected quasi-topos","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]}]